{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/299272-inhuman-scions","id":299272,"title":"Inhuman Scions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-01T14:25:34-07:00","id":299272,"title":"Inhuman Scions","content":"Somewhat new to Scion, though I've gone through the books a bit. I'm curious- are there any rules for the gods having inhuman or at least inhuman appearing offspring? Or are such creatures the sole province of titanspawn? I've seen the description of Donnie Rhodes in God as him possessing wings? At what point would a Scion begin to manifest such inhuman manifestations of his divinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T15:40:01-07:00","id":299396,"title":"","content":"Unusual Alteration immediately opens up inhuman options.<br /> With storyteller approval you can play anything that looks inhuman, with the appropriate social consequences for your appearance (depending on what that is).<br /> Some storytellers have no problem with the other half of your parentage being a legendary creature of some sort, while other storytellers consider it taboo.<br /> There was even a Scion game advertised on here a while back where everyone played animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T17:47:06-07:00","id":299505,"title":"","content":"As I understand the concept, a Scion's form is influenced by the legends that surround him. In other words, he takes on the traits of how the mortals believe him to be. While it is possible to have unusual appearances, they start to manifest around Demi God and higher levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then again, maybe I misinterpreted that completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T19:31:14-07:00","id":299542,"title":"","content":"Just a small point; I thought that Donnie Rhodes was depicted wearing the Daedalus device.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T20:35:11-07:00","id":299606,"title":"","content":"Animal Feature (Bird), which Donnie has, would allow him to have wings. So Legend 6. But I agree that he is most likely just being pictured with his relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T01:12:05-07:00","id":299810,"title":"","content":"Makes you wonder about the gods whose appearance has never actually been human in the first place doesn't it? Like most of the egyptian pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T15:38:15-08:00","id":301546,"title":"","content":"Many of them would have been the children of two gods or of Titan avatars and could have been born with enough Legend to have Animal Feature already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T00:28:36-08:00","id":304236,"title":"","content":"Yeah, during the span of Hero - God in First Edition, Seth Farrow gradually became more snake-like until he had the hooded head of a Cobra in God. Though in this upcoming edition, there may be inhuman creature PCs in Origins that may become new Scions when Hero comes up as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T04:35:42-08:00","id":307328,"title":"","content":"I believe Scion would mean half god, half mortal. If the latter is anything but a mortal, then it's a creature, immortals, minor Gods and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T07:59:36-08:00","id":307433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/299272-inhuman-scions?p=307328#post307328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Scion would mean half god, half mortal. If the latter is anything but a mortal, then it's a creature, immortals, minor Gods and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, it doesn't always. According to a sidebar in the Deva chapter of Scion: Companion, sometime two gods will produce a Scion together, which they usually leave in the World with parents who have time to raise them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T09:02:23-08:00","id":307460,"title":"","content":"I believe that specifically requires at least one of them to take on mortal form, making them temporarily... mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T11:12:35-08:00","id":307618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/299272-inhuman-scions?p=307460#post307460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that specifically requires at least one of them to take on mortal form, making them temporarily... mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only the first option. The second explicitly mentions that gods can sometimes produce Scions even without one of them going Avatar.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found the quote. &quot;Un-divine child: One God plus one God does not always equal another God. Sometimes the child of two divine parents turns out to be mortal. What do you about that? Well, the child\u2019s parents might decide it is best for the baby to grow up with normal parents, and whoever has time for the Visitation can claim dibs on the divine parentage. Don\u2019t forget the Adopted Parent option either: There is no greater story arc for a Scion than a quest to determine his true heritage. And what could stop other Gods from swooping in and claiming the orphaned Scion as her own?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Exact Quote 11-09-2014, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T11:18:11-08:00","id":307619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/299272-inhuman-scions?p=307328#post307328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Scion would mean half god, half mortal. If the latter is anything but a mortal, then it's a creature, immortals, minor Gods and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your storyteller can always decide that some other race have mortal members. Or just not care at all because they are sufficiently close to humans in appearance.<br /> Alfar are popular around here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:20:06-08:00","id":307816,"title":"","content":"My Loki-Spawn picked up all the shapeshifting stuff before demi-god and she was growing more devilish every time I advanced her Epic Appearance (which was originaly divine ugliness because there was just something subtly, horribly wrong with her even before she started developing horns).....having all the shapeshifting stuff meant that even her gender was rather fluid.<br /> <br /> <br /> My Benten daughter didn't delve too deeply into her spider connections (well, almost all her magic spells were related to taking advantage of the swarms of spiders that followed (and often rode on) her, but she didn't get past Animal Communication and her Appearance was based on being supernaturally adorable. I re-worked the defensive Do Not Want boon into a D'Awww boon where people and animals would hesitate to hurt someone so cute and there was a Pang of Conscience which took dice off attempts to ambush her giving her a better chance to catch them at it, basically, they would hesitate before attacking her so it was easier to see the ambush coming.<br /> <br /> Most of my others lacked inhuman appearances.<br /> <br /> I gave up on modeling my school girl Medusa girl in scion. For one thing, the mythology in Scion does not go with the mythology I used for her origin (the idea of Medusa's pre-Greek partiarchal demonization of her, when she was a Goddess of Rebirth, Transformation and Death). The healing aspects are relatively easy to pull off, the petrifying gaze (which was a temporary effect for her) was more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:26:01-08:00","id":307818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/299272-inhuman-scions?p=307619#post307619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your storyteller can always decide that some other race have mortal members. Or just not care at all because they are sufficiently close to humans in appearance.<br /> Alfar are popular around here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of my Susano'o daughter's long term goals was to create a way for the more inhuman creatures around the world to be accepted by humanity so they could stop hiding. By extension she expected several of the most powerful members of each race to be officially accepted as gods whether the established pantheons liked it or not (she was big on equality).<br /> <br /> I only got her to Legend 4 before a disagreement between a GM and another player resulted in killing the campaign. At the time, her only plan was the admittedly weak idea of using the high ranked boons for making animal and plant people and faking a discovery of cosmetic genetic modification. (she was a stage magician though, so she would have needed help selling that)<br /> <br /> I expect some people would try to stop her on the fear that her plan would reduce thousands of the lesser supernaturals to being pure mortals (which she wasn't thinking about.)<br /> <br /> Her primary motivation is that people shouldn't have to hide what they are and that these other immortals should be accepted as gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T15:30:29-08:00","id":329599,"title":"","content":"Isn't fenrir a scion by extension? Or is he considered a god?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T16:03:48-08:00","id":329614,"title":"","content":"In my &quot;point-of view&quot; Fenrir was an old god that taught humanity how to hunt as a group and as a result humans became more successful hunters. (A lot of old hunter gods way back when) He later became &quot;demonized&quot; to justify this upstart Norse pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T17:52:05-08:00","id":329692,"title":"","content":"well there aint much in the norse mythos itself that suggested fenris was inherently evil, just that Odin had a bad sensation. He kinda made his own problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T03:37:24-08:00","id":329983,"title":"","content":"The prophecy wasn't Odins(he doesnt really do that). Pretty much all the poems/songs/stories that ever mention him say he is a vehicle of destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T06:25:30-08:00","id":330059,"title":"","content":"Yeah they say it but there is no real evidence for it. Just that it was shown in a vision and the gods became fearful when he grew massive. He's apparently sentient enough to play games with them (as the first two bindings were to him). Someone once mentioned to me they knew local tales of fenrir being a ferocious beast, but they never relayed those to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T07:27:22-08:00","id":330109,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I actually haven't heard any tales of Hr\u00f3\u00f0vitnir(Glory-Wolf) actually doing anything until after he is imprisoned in a self-fulfilling prophesy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:26:59-08:00","id":330177,"title":"","content":"All we have for lore on the fen-dweller was written by a Christian 200+ years after his country's christianization. While true, he is mentioned in the seers poem, the only real details we have are from Snorri (who could be argued as being a closet Odin cultist and incredibly biased anyway.). The lore itself makes it look as the gods brought their own vengeance upon them through their oath breaking, which is a common theme in old norse mythos.<br /> <br /> edit: not intending to disagree with people's personal views of how the mythos works, just suggesting that what is written is not necessarily what it is. If anyone has an example of localized tales involving the fen-dweller then by all means!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 12-04-2014, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:56:36-08:00","id":330897,"title":"","content":"Theres no &quot;real evidence&quot; for anything though. At that point you're just making things up. Which is completely fine for your game or your own personal views, but isnt a good place to argue about how things &quot;really were.&quot; As scholars we can only use the information we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T15:24:01-08:00","id":335520,"title":"","content":"Most of the monsters in Norse Mythos represent natural phenomena. They considered the elements the most dangerous thing and their myths reflect that. Their monsters are less likely to be demonizations than the monsters of Greek myths. The Norse were assimilationist in religious habit. They tended to accept any culture that proved itself to have strength. Which is why you have the Vanir joining the Aesir rather than being destroyed by them. <br /> <br /> But yeah, the fights against the giants, jormungandr, Fenris and so on were most likely metaphors for the slow conquering of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T20:24:45-08:00","id":336668,"title":"","content":"I actually think the Vanir/Aesir merger was representative of two cultures merging during the migration era. I've seen this whole argument before, but I don't know that that is the end all be all to it. Yes we see metaphors today, but is that because we're looking for them, or are they really there? Could the Fenris wolf not be something made to just be an epic end? Who doesn't want to go down fighting something so badass that even gods can't stand against it? Hell Ragnarok features how many cataclysmic events? Surtr's sword that's brighter then the sun and cuts through the heavens? Possible meteor. Theres a flood of biblical proportions, fire covering the whole earth, epic winter, famine, war (major fratricide and incest too apparently) and giant monsters that are as epic to the common man as beasts like Grendel from Beowulf. I think at this point it's less about representing something specific, and more about being incredibly badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T07:15:26-08:00","id":336989,"title":"","content":"Eh, if you have to make up a way for the world to end, making it as metal as possible is not the worst way to go about it. But I think we're a bit off topic here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}